            "content": "Layer 5 of the reasoning-effort stack. Compaction inherits effort; every surface\nthat records `modelId` now records the effort beside it.\n\n## Compaction inherits — and why that's a cache decision\n\n`CompactionService` runs fire-and-forget immediately after a completed turn\n*specifically* so the call lands inside the provider's prompt-cache TTL, and\n`buildCompactionRequest` reproduces that turn's exact system prompt and message\nprefix to hit it (`compaction.service.ts:101`). Sending a different effort than\nthe prefix was built under invalidates the message blocks that request shape\nexists to reuse — Anthropic documents effort changes as always invalidating\nthem, and OpenAI effort changes are reported to cause full-prefix misses.\n\nSo this is about not throwing away a cache hit, not about summary quality.\n\n**Transition compaction uses the SOURCE run's effort**, not the incoming turn's.\nIt reuses the source model and the source snapshot's prompt, so that is the\nprefix whose cache is at stake — and the incoming effort was validated against a\n*different* model's declared levels and need not exist on this one.\n\nThe value is captured once, where the existing guard has already narrowed\n`sourceRun`:\n\n```ts\nconst sourceEffort = state.sourceRun.effort ?? undefined;\n```\n\nBoth the `summarize` call and the compaction telemetry read that single binding,\nso the sent value and the recorded value cannot disagree — and passing the\nincoming turn's effort isn't expressible in that function at all.\n\n**Title generation is untouched.** Different model, own prompt, no shared prefix,\nso no cache argument reaches it. Its signatures carry no effort parameter, so the\nabsence is structural rather than conventional.\n\n## Effort travels with modelId\n\n| surface | carries effort |\n| --- | --- |\n| `TurnTelemetry` + both writers + structured log | ✅ |\n| `RunResponse` | ✅ |\n| `ContextReceiptResponse` | ✅ run-sourced, outside the snapshot hashes |\n| `CompactionStatsResponse` | ✅ |\n| `model.requested` event | ✅ |\n| `ActiveRunResponse` | ✗ — carries no `modelId` |\n| `SharedChatMessageResponse` | ✗ — carries no `usage` |\n\nThe two exclusions are now pinned by a test asserting their exact key sets, so\nbroadening that boundary has to be deliberate rather than incidental.\n\n## Two specced tests deliberately not written\n\nBoth would be tautologies that pass against *any* implementation, and layer 4's\nreview flagged that exact class as a defect:\n\n- **Title abstention** — `maybeGenerateTitle({chatId, userId, userText})` and\n  `requestTitle(client, userText)` have no effort parameter. No path exists for a\n  run's effort to reach that call; the type system already guarantees it.\n- **No-recompute** — nothing reads configuration to rebuild a persisted `usage`,\n  receipt, or event value. The execution half is already pinned by the layer-4\n  test that sends a stored level the current catalog would reject.\n\nFlagging these rather than burying them: if either is judged genuinely fallible,\nthe test should be written.\n\n## Verification\n\n`turbo run build --filter=api`, `api lint`, `api typecheck`, `api test` (1529),\n`api test:integration` (426 passed / 0 failed), `web build`. `openapi.json` and\nthe Orval bindings regenerated and committed.\n\nStacked on #590. `effort/finalize` — CHANGELOG, `/opsx:sync`, `/opsx:archive` —\nis the last layer.\n",
