            "command": "cd /home/leon0399/.herdr/worktrees/llame/assistant-efford-and-params; git status --porcelain; git add -A; git commit -q -F - <<'EOF'\nfeat(web): surface reasoning effort in the chat UI\n\nFour surfaces, all reading the effort the api already records beside\n`modelId`:\n\n- the turn badge below a message reads `Model · effort · 34.07s`, with effort\n  dropping out entirely for a turn that carried none rather than showing a\n  placeholder;\n- the hover telemetry card gains an `at effort` row indented beneath Model,\n  the way `of which cached` sits beneath Input — it qualifies the row above\n  rather than standing as a peer fact;\n- the effective-context sidebar gains an Effort row beneath Model, omitted\n  when the receipt carries none, because an empty cell would read as \"effort\n  was none\" rather than \"no effort applied\";\n- the composer gains an effort selector between the model picker and send.\n\nThe selector renders NOTHING when the selected model declares no `reasoning`\nobject — that absence is the api saying this model takes no effort, so a\ndisabled or empty control would misstate it. It brings its own leading seam so\nthe composer pill collapses back to two cells instead of leaving a divider\nwith nothing after it.\n\nLevels are rendered verbatim. The model contract states a client must not\nderive meaning, magnitude, or ordering from a level's text, so no token is\nmapped to friendlier prose; the array's ORDER is the only scale, which is why\na slider expresses it and a select would not. The scale's ends are labelled by\nthe trade-off (Faster/Smarter) rather than by the extreme level names, which\nare per-model tokens and would be wrong on the next model.\n\nThe slider is the shadcn registry component added via the CLI, not\nhand-rolled. Its bold treatment lives in the consumer through the primitive's\n`data-slot` hooks, so no other slider inherits the emphasis and the vendored\nfile stays unforked apart from the JSDoc this repo requires.\n\nKept achromatic deliberately: DESIGN.md §12.1 records \"no brand hue\" as an\nintentionally undecided question, so painting this control blue would resolve\na documented open decision by drift. Emphasis comes from weight and contrast.\n\nSelection is re-seeded from the model's own `defaultEffort` whenever the model\nchanges, because vocabularies differ and a level carried over may not exist —\nfalling back by position would be worse, since position means nothing across\nmodels. The send path reads effort through a ref for the same reason `modelId`\ndoes: the transport closure is created once and would otherwise pin the first\nturn's level for the life of the chat.\n\nRefs #584\nEOF\ngit log --oneline -1",
